# v2.2.2:
- Added vanilla government power cost for Auto-Grant Urban Rights
- Add a Minimum Government Power setting that stops auto-granting before your government power drops below it, you can also enable unrestricted tools in CMF settings->Remove Government Power Cost to disable it (mainly for my own testing)
- Auto-Food and the Auto-Urbanize ignore list now hides RGO's you don't have
- Auto-Expand RGO is now disabled in locations where Auto-Food is active (redundant)
- Fix the settings "reset to default" button not restoring the correct starting values for some lists
- Fix Auto-Urbanize queuing a duplicate rank upgrade while one is already under construction
- Fix mass-mode Auto-Food locations not showing in the Breadbaskets map mode
- Fix the Auto-Expand Metric sometimes not applying correctly after switching it
- The auto-expand tooltip now shows when the building auto-expand feature is turned off
- Reworked construction queuing to run more reliably

# v2.2.1:
- Fix broken translations
- Fix edge case where auto-expand and auto-upgrade, both queuing at the same exact time, constructing two levels instead of 1.

# v2.2.0:
- Complete core logic overhaul: construction decisions now use the game's real cost and income numbers instead of the mod's own estimates
- New Auto-Expand Metric setting: gate auto-expand of buildings and RGOs on Tax Income, Profit, ROI (Tax), or ROI (Profit)
- Auto-expand selections now automatically transfer to the replacement building type when the original becomes obsolete
- Auto-expand buttons are now hidden on obsolete buildings
- Ported building view UI changes from Glorp UI (so I don't have to duplicate work)
- The production view now shows Return on Investment (also added to Glorp UI)
- Auto-expand tooltips now show the actual construction cost and how much gold you need before the expand will queue
- More accurate cost and income estimates for RGO auto-expand
- Added 7 more urban rights to the Auto-Grant Urban Rights list
- The Found Town and Found City buildings now cost approximately the same as upgrading the location rank directly
- Reorganized the settings window
- Removed wool from Auto-Food since wool no longer produces food
- Fix buildings that cost religious influence or other special currencies being built without paying
- Fix auto-upgrade queueing duplicate upgrades for buildings already being upgraded (could construct extra levels)
- Fix the auto-expand button showing on foreign-owned buildings in the build menu
- Fix the auto-expand button and icon sometimes not appearing
- Fix more error log spam


# v2.1.3:
- Fix one broken icon
- Fix error log spam

# v2.1.2:
- Redid 1.3 integration (this time less rushed) with the mod more naturally integrating into the vanilla UI
- Auto-Urbanize will no longer urbanize locations where Mass Auto-Food is enabled.

# v2.1.1:
- Many fixes for v1.3

# v2.1.0:
- Updated for EU5 v1.3 "Pavia"
- Auto-expand buttons now use the game's new built-in auto-expand icon and checkbox
- Integrated with the game's Automation panel: its "Auto-Expand Buildings" and "Auto-Expand R.G.O." entries now stay in sync with Construction Manager's on/off, and their button opens the Construction Manager settings instead of the production view

# v2.0.2:
- Fix some broken non-english localizations
- Prevent auto-build from queueing up building levels beyond the cap
- Prevent auto-upgrade from queueing upgrades for in-progress buildings

# v2.0.1:
- Change max gold reserve to 100k
- Change default min discount to 0%
- Correct some localizations
- Prevent granting town rights where the requirements aren't met
- Correct min profit (was checking the profit of all levels, rather than per level), note that it currently doesn't apply before a building has a level constructed due to engine limitations

# v2.0.0:
[h1]New Automation:[/h1]
[list]
 [*][b]Auto-Upgrade All Buildings[/b]: Upgrades obsolete buildings to their next tier across your country, regardless of whether auto-expand is on for that building.
 [*][b]Auto-Food[/b]: Builds food-producing RGOs and food buildings in rural locations, picking the highest marginal food output. Can be enabled on a per location, or through a mass toggle based on your selected criteria (i.e. wheat on a river).
 [*][b]Auto-Urbanize[/b]: Promotes rural settlements to towns and towns to cities each month. Sub-toggles per tier, plus an RGO ignore list (gold, gems, spices, etc.).
 [*][b]Auto-Build Capital[/b]: Constructs your capital-only buildings (royal court, supreme court, war college, admiralty, chancery, parliament, etc.) when conditions allow.
 [*][b]Auto-Grant Urban Rights[/b]: Grants enabled urban rights to your cities and megalopolises in priority order.
[/list]

[h1]New Filters:[/h1]
[list]
 [*]Tax Base and Wealth (with and without control scaling)
 [*]Building Levels Filled (relative to supported cap)
 [*]Production Efficiency and Building Level
 [*]Food Potential Per RGO Level
 [*]R.G.O. Value
 [*]Number of Locations Per Province
 [*]Attacker Penalty (from terrain)
 [*]Good Migration Candidate (non-city under 30k pops)
[/list]

[h1]New Map Modes:[/h1]
[list]
 [*][b]Breadbaskets[/b]: Highlights locations where auto-food is enabled.
 [*][b]Food Potential Per RGO Level[/b]: Colors locations by natural food potential. Factors in rgo, terrain, vegetation, climate, named static modifiers, water access, and assumed-max bonuses from windmill, farming village, and irrigation systems etc. Essentially it shows you the locations with the highest possible food output.
[/list]

[h1]New Integration:[/h1]
[list]
 [*]Integrates with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3601047146]Glorp UI[/url] - Load Glorp UI after/below Construction Manager
 [*]Integrated with the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3692202776]Community Mod Framework[/url]
[/list]

[h1]New Requirements:[/h1]
Now requires the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3692202776]Community Mod Framework[/url].
